menuconfig CAGENT_ADDONS
    bool "cAGENT addons: node protocol and MCP bridge"
    default n
    help
      Optional addon package for cAGENT: OpenClaw Node protocol
      (multi-device collaboration, contest task B) and MCP gateway
      bridge (contest task C).

      Layering rule: the node protocol layer (CAGENT_ADDONS_NODE)
      builds without CAGENT so cAGENT-less node-role devices (e.g.
      demos/sensor_node) can use it; the gateway/glue and MCP modules
      depend on CAGENT public API only.

      See openvela_smarthome/docs/cagent-addons-design-rev2.md.

if CAGENT_ADDONS

menu "Modules"

config CAGENT_ADDONS_NODE
    bool "OpenClaw Node protocol layer (WebSocket + frames)"
    default y
    help
      Platform-independent protocol layer: WebSocket framing and
      OpenClaw Node frame codec. Does not depend on CAGENT.
    select NETUTILS_CJSON

config CAGENT_ADDONS_NODE_CLIENT
    bool "Node role (connect to a gateway, serve invokes)"
    default n
    depends on CAGENT_ADDONS_NODE
    help
      Node-role endpoint: connects to a gateway over WebSocket,
      answers connect.challenge, serves node.invoke requests from a
      local command table. No CAGENT dependency.

config CAGENT_ADDONS_NODE_GATEWAY
    bool "Gateway role (accept nodes, expose remote tools to cAGENT)"
    default n
    depends on CAGENT_ADDONS_NODE && CAGENT
    help
      Gateway role: accepts node connections, registers node tools
      into a cAGENT agent as node_<id>_<command>, dispatches invokes.

config CAGENT_ADDONS_MCP
    bool "Standard MCP Streamable HTTP client"
    default n
    depends on CAGENT
    select NETUTILS_CJSON
    help
      Standard MCP Streamable HTTP tools-only client. Connects directly
      to one configured MCP Server, runs initialize/tools/list/tools/call,
      and registers allowlisted external tools into cAGENT as
      mcp_<server>_<tool>. Does not support stdio, SSE streams or OAuth.

endmenu

menu "Capacity limits"

